Backport of theoremlp/rules_multitool@cb9b69e, "fix: don't add transitive hubs
to direct deps" (#115), which is merged upstream but not in any release as of
1.11.1.

Without it the extension classifies a hub declared by any module in the graph
as a direct dependency of the root, so a root module that uses multitool as a
dev dependency -- as this one does, to keep actionlint out of the graph its
consumers resolve -- collides with the non-dev hub that cgrindel_bazel_starlib
declares, reaching us through rules_bazel_integration_test:

    Error in extension_metadata: in root_module_direct_dev_deps:
    entry 'multitool' is also in root_module_direct_deps

Drop this patch, and the single_version_override in MODULE.bazel, once a
release containing the fix is in the registry.

--- a/multitool/extension.bzl
+++ b/multitool/extension.bzl
@@ -26,10 +26,8 @@
             else:
                 lockfiles[h.hub_name] = [h.lockfile]

-            if not module_ctx.is_dev_dependency(h):
-                root_module_direct_deps[h.hub_name] = 1
-            else:
-                root_module_direct_dev_deps[h.hub_name] = 1
+            if mod.is_root:
+                (root_module_direct_dev_deps if module_ctx.is_dev_dependency(h) else root_module_direct_deps)[h.hub_name] = 1

     # ensure _DEFAULT_HUB_NAME is present in non-dev and dev deps
     # when non-dev and dev deps are non-empty.
